The static review finds no task-answer oracle or execution-bypassing proof rule: the big-step semantics does execute the submitted constructor tree. Its source does, however, call `substrString` on reachable empty-slice boundaries even though the installed K documentation says that primitive is only defined for `start < end`; this explains the preserved LLVM crash. I’m treating that as a backend/definedness evidence gap, not as an unsound-rule allegation, because I have no false conclusion witness and the fresh Haskell executions match the submitted Python. Next is the required fresh false-result mutation.
